  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, identifying outcomes with probability > 0.5 as probable — is not present in the verbal report. The individual does not consider any outcome as probable, as both probabilities (0.1% and 0.2%) are far below 0.5. Therefore, the individual does not apply the rule of the decision reason. The justification provided (desiring to take a chance on a large win) is based on risk preference and emotional appeal, not on calculating or comparing the average number of probable outcomes. Since the individual neither identifies probable outcomes nor uses the rule to compare lotteries based on such outcomes, the decision reason was not used. The assessment is therefore 0.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
